{
  "name": "amoo-web",
  "version": "0.1.0",
  "private": true,
  "scripts": {
    "dev": "next dev --webpack",
    "build": "node scripts/validate-env.mjs && next build --webpack",
    "start": "next start",
    "lint": "eslint",
    "typecheck": "tsc --noEmit",
    "test": "tsx --test \"lib/__tests__/*.test.ts\"",
    "test:e2e": "playwright test",
    "validate-env": "node scripts/validate-env.mjs"
  },
  "dependencies": {
    "@sentry/nextjs": "^10.68.0",
    "dompurify": "^3.4.12",
    "jose": "^6.2.4",
    "lucide-react": "^1.24.0",
    "next": "16.2.11",
    "react": "19.2.4",
    "react-dom": "19.2.4"
  },
  "//overrides": [
    "Both entries patch vulnerabilities that reach us only through next's own",
    "dependency tree, so bumping next alone cannot clear them:",
    "  sharp   <0.35.0  — libvips CVE-2026-33327/33328/35590/35591 (high).",
    "                     Used by next/image optimisation, which this app does",
    "                     use, including for remote images.",
    "  postcss <8.5.10  — XSS via unescaped </style> in stringify output",
    "                     (GHSA-qx2v-qp2m-jg93, moderate).",
    "Remove an entry once next depends on a patched version by itself.",
    "`npm audit fix --force` is NOT the answer here: it proposes next@9.3.3."
  ],
  "overrides": {
    "sharp": "^0.35.3",
    "postcss": "^8.5.10"
  },
  "devDependencies": {
    "@playwright/test": "^1.62.0",
    "@tailwindcss/postcss": "^4",
    "@types/dompurify": "^3.0.5",
    "@types/node": "^20",
    "@types/react": "^19",
    "@types/react-dom": "^19",
    "eslint": "^9",
    "eslint-config-next": "16.2.11",
    "tailwindcss": "^4",
    "tsx": "^4.23.1",
    "typescript": "^5"
  }
}
